A1. A German life saver. ~ MORATORIUM
A10. "Of all sad words of tongue or pen the saddest" is this. ~ ALAS
A14. Females that are easily fleeced. ~ EWES
A15. Divinity food. (Don't confuse this with fudge.) ~ MANNA
A16. What every mother wishes to keep from her young son's ears. ~ DIRT
A17. The kind of a lamb that is easily roasted. ~ MEEK
A18. This can represent almost anything. ~ AGENT
A19. Arithmetic problem—Take three fifths of a square or three fourths of the area, and the answer is .025 of an acre. ~ ARE
A20. Here is where we are giving you the advantage. ~ ODDS
A21. At this point—be careful. ~ HERE
A22. Pardon the mistake, and we hope it is the only one in the puzzle. ~ ERROR
A24. The way the Prince of Wales rides when he plays polo. ~ ASTRIDE
A26. This sounds like a merger of some kind ~ WE
A27. When the sartorial artists do this some one is going to have a perfect fit. ~ ALTER
A32. An explanation for this would be useless ~ VOID
A33. This is not Scotch but just attempt to draw on it and it will tighten up immediately. ~ NOOSE
A34. Just keep the change please. (You're welcome.) ~ CENT
A35. A subdivision of Los Angeles. ~ LOS
A38. This lady supplied moonshine to the Romans. ~ DIANA
A39. They are often canned after they leave this. ~ POD
A40. There is a lot of science in this. It will need study. ~ OLOGY
A42. Don't get stuck here. It is deep and treacherous. ~ UNDERTOW
A44. What the poet used to quoth. ~ RAVEN
A45. They have these to burn down in the editor's office (abbr.). ~ MSS
A46. Here is something to annoy. ~ IRK
A47. You will be going some if you get a fine sentence from this. ~ SPEED
A48. When the goldenrod is yellow and the corn is turning brown, These are the blowouts that you hear around the town. ~ SNEEZES
A52. This might stand for Henry but it never did for Lizzie. ~ HE
A54. This will give you the time of your life. ~ AGE
A55. An old-fashioned yard. ~ ELL
A56. Something heroic. ~ EPIC
A59. This used to be one of the garden spots of the world. ~ EDEN
A61. A French tutor. ~ ABBE
A62. What's in a name? There are 4 letters in this girl's name. ~ CORA
A63. Why should this one worry—it has a perfectly good bed, is constantly being fed, and puts its deposits in a bank? ~ RIVER
A65. The bigger this is the more we are going to starve. ~ CROP
A66. We got this from a wise old bird. ~ HOOT
A67. If you are going to make this you will have to begin. ~ START
A68. A man of letters and his most brilliant one was scarlet. ~ HAWTHORNE

D1. A little remembrance for the wife's birthday. ~ MEMORANDUM
D2. What bond salesmen have done for a living since the depression. ~ OWED
D3. A musical pipe. ~ REED
D4. What the younger generation does that the older generation must answer for. ~ ASKS
D5. There is a lot of western capital in this. ~ OMAHA
D6. Something aviators should never fly into (plur.). ~ RAGES
D7. The way the fish looked after it was caught. ~ INERT
D8. What the crash did to the man at the wheel. ~ UNNERVED
D9. A good thing to slip on after taking a bath. ~ MAT
D10. You can get this by sending to the station to which you are listening. ~ AD
D11. The woman who advertises she is 39. ~ LIAR
D12. A point of direction. ~ ARROW
D13. What a meter that goes around a block registers. ~ STERE
D22. You can always get good returns from these. ~ EDITORS
D23. A Crown that is a standard commodity and a source of power. ~ RED
D25. This is only a small matter. ~ ION
D28. The roast he got when he brought a friend home for dinner (plur.). ~ LOINS
D29. The tools Mother Nature uses to make mushrooms. ~ TOADS
D30. An old slave that has always been faithful to puzzle makers. ~ ESNE
D31. This is all they were doing when they said they were raising Cain. ~ REARING
D34. The belle of the barnyard. ~ COW
D35. It may help some if we tell you it is blind. ~ LOVE
D36. An old part of the building that is molding. ~ OGEE
D37. When big fellows get together this is what they sometimes make. ~ SYNDICATE
D39. To stir up a flame. ~ POKE
D41. This is a catty thing to do. ~ LAP
D43. Believe it or not, this wears more in the summer than in the winter. ~ TREE
D48. This is comparatively wise. ~ SANER
D49. This animal must have just come out of its pen. ~ ZEBRA
D50. A crook that can easily work in a crowd. ~ ELBOW
D51. What John did while his wife was listening to a sermon. ~ SLEPT
D52. All that he owns is this. ~ HERS
D53. You will get this at the turning of the tide. ~ EDIT
D56. Nature's encore. ~ ECHO
D57. The kind of a fish that has human qualities. ~ POOR
D58. A scorcher. ~ IRON
D60. This one has died so many times that au-topsy is suggested. ~ EVA
D61. A preface to himmel. ~ ACH
D64. In order to make this right we had to reduce it. ~ RT


